@startuml

title 11. Status history, audit fields and deletion rules

hide circle
skinparam linetype ortho

enum StatusHistoryEntityType {
	purchase
	inventory_document
	production_order
}

entity StatusHistory {
	* id: int
	--
	* entityType: StatusHistoryEntityType
	* entityId: int
	oldStatus: string(100)?
	* newStatus: string(100)
	comment: text?
	* changedAt: DateTimeImmutable
	changedBy: User?
	* store: Store
}

Store ||--o{ StatusHistory : has status logs
User |o--o{ StatusHistory : changes status
StatusHistoryEntityType ||--o{ StatusHistory : classifies

note right of StatusHistory
  Current project status:
  - StatusHistory is not implemented.
  - Many business entities already have status and audit fields.
  - Status changes are not logged centrally.

  Required behavior:
  - Every business status transition creates a history row.
  - entityType + entityId are used intentionally for MVP flexibility.
  - Application code validates that entityId exists for the type.
  - History rows are append-only.
  - UI should show status timeline on Purchase,
    InventoryDocument and ProductionOrder pages.
  - Order uses dedicated OrderHistory from stage 05.1,
    because its timeline must store all actions, not only status changes.
  - Payment has audit requirements, but no business status workflow
    in the current model, so it is not part of StatusHistory yet.
end note

note bottom
  Shared deletion/audit policy:

  Soft delete / archive:
  - Product, Category, Unit, Warehouse, Customer, Supplier,
    ProductPrice and InventoryReason keep historical readability
    through deletedAt/status rather than destructive removal.

  Never hard delete once they have business impact:
  - Order
  - Purchase
  - InventoryDocument
  - Payment
  - ProductionOrder
  - InventoryDocumentLine
  - StockMovement
  - WarehouseStockBatch
  - StockReservation
  - StatusHistory
  - OrderHistory

  Draft-only exception:
  - A draft business document may be hard deleted only when
    business rules allow it and it has no posted movements,
    payments or other dependent history.

  Audit fields:
  - createdBy/updatedBy/canceledBy/postedBy/startedBy/completedBy
    are historical audit data, not a permission model.
  - Fill them consistently in services or subscribers.
end note

note bottom
  Suggested implementation steps:

  1. Add StatusHistory entity, enum and repository.
  2. Add StatusHistoryService::record().
  3. Keep Order on dedicated OrderHistory from stage 05.1.
  4. Update Purchase transition service first.
  5. Then update InventoryDocument and ProductionOrder services.
  6. Add reusable Twig component for generic status timeline rendering.
  7. Add tests that every generic transition writes history exactly once.
  8. Add deletion-policy tests around posted documents and history.
end note

@enduml
